:"src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java-src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java--21560:21590","promptId":"#HF0S9","srcPath":"src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java","dstPath":"src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":21560,"endPos":21590,"startLine":495,"startLineOffset":93,"endLine":495,"endLineOffset":123,"length":31}]},{"id":"src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java-src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java--25417:25447","promptId":"#DXYDC","srcPath":"src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java","dstPath":"src/test/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploaderTest.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":25417,"endPos":25447,"startLine":583,"startLineOffset":93,"endLine":583,"endLineOffset":123,"length":31}]}]},{"comment":"The comment change from \"It\u0027s a programming error to reference a file that has not been uploaded.\" to \"It\u0027s a programming error to reference a file that has not had the opportunity to be uploaded.\" is grammatically correct but less clear. The original comment more directly conveys the intent that referencing an unuploaded file is an error, while the new comment introduces ambiguity about what \"opportunity\" means in this context.","nodes":[{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-18905:18980-19231:19326","promptId":"#QAC0Z","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":18905,"endPos":18980,"startLine":521,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":521,"endLineOffset":83,"length":76}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":19231,"endPos":19326,"startLine":533,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":533,"endLineOffset":103,"length":96}]}]},{"comment":"The logic for determining whether a path should be uploaded has been moved from `shouldUpload` to `readPathMetadata`. However, the condition for omitting paths when `remoteBuildEventUploadMode` is `MINIMAL` now includes checking `file.type`, which was not present in the original `isBuildOrTestLog` method. This change might lead to inconsistencies if `file.type` does not always reflect the type of log files correctly, especially since test logs are checked using a regex pattern.","nodes":[{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java--7624:8441","promptId":"#C8X7D","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7624,"endPos":8441,"startLine":202,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":223,"endLineOffset":5,"length":818}]},{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-10449:10602-","promptId":"#VFJ6X","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10449,"endPos":10602,"startLine":289,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":291,"endLineOffset":5,"length":154}],"dstChanges":[]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":223,"start_side":"RIGHT","start_line":202,"line":223,"comment_lines":["[][202]","[][203]","[][204]","[][205]","[][206]","[][207]","[][208]","[][209]","[][210]","[][211]","[][212]","[][213]","[][214]","[][215]","[][216]","[][217]","[][218]","[][219]","[][220]","[][221]","[][222]","[][223]"],"review_comment":["I\u0027m having a hard time trying to understand what functionally changes in this PR. What do we save by exiting early here, considering that we\u0027re still calling `digestUtil.compute`?","I find myself asking the same question. This went through a number of iterations, as I discovered more and more requirements that incrementally eliminated any kind of potential optimisation.\r\n\r\nI\u0027m going to close this. There is room for improvement in the bytestream uploader (I had a stab at some in #23252 but hit a NPE I could not track down, at face value the area seems like it would benefit from a refactor and perhaps alignment across full and minimal upload modes).","FWIW, I don\u0027t think the uploader should be digesting files at all; all output files have already been digested (and the digests cached in memory as a `FileArtifactValue`) during action execution, so we should figure out a way to plumb that data into the uploader.","Some spawn intermediate outputs might not be stored, though."],"path":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","id":20501,"created_at":"2024-08-30T11:55:02Z","original_position":34,"side":"RIGHT","position":34,"original_start_line":202,"submitted_on_commit":"ab672a32fa3004d4c14790dd571f1b9379d9201b","diff_hunk":"@@ -201,6 +199,29 @@ public DigestFunction.Value getDigestFunction() {\n   private PathMetadata readPathMetadata(Path path, LocalFile file) throws IOException {\n     DigestUtil digestUtil \u003d new DigestUtil(xattrProvider, path.getFileSystem().getDigestFunction());\n \n+    if (remoteBuildEventUploadMode \u003d\u003d RemoteBuildEventUploadMode.MINIMAL) {\n+      // Omit all unimportant paths\n+      if (!(\n+        // Logs (regex needed for test logs as they lack a dedicated `LocalFileType`)\n+        TEST_LOG_PATTERN.matcher(path.getPathString()).matches()\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.LOG\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.PERFORMANCE_LOG\n+        // std(out|err)\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.STDOUT\n+        || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.STDERR\n+      )) {\n+        return new PathMetadata(\n+            path,\n+            digestUtil.compute(path),\n+            /* directory\u003d */ false,\n+            /* symlink\u003d */ false,\n+            /* remote\u003d */ false,\n+            /* omitted\u003d */ true,\n+            /* isBuildToolLog\u003d */ false,\n+            digestUtil.getDigestFunction());\n+      }\n+    }","submitted_start_line":202,"submitted_line":223},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The new condition for omitting paths includes checking `file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.LOG || file.type \u003d\u003d LocalFileType.PERFORMANCE_LOG`. This is redundant with the existing check in `PathMetadata` constructor where `isBuildToolLog` is set based on these types. Consider consolidating this logic to avoid duplication and potential inconsistencies.","nodes":[{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java--7624:8441","promptId":"#C8X7D","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7624,"endPos":8441,"startLine":202,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":223,"endLineOffset":5,"length":818}]}]},{"comment":"The logic for determining whether a path should be uploaded has been moved from `shouldUpload` to `readPathMetadata`. However, the condition for omitting paths when `remoteBuildEventUploadMode` is `MINIMAL` now includes checking `file.type`, which was not present in the original `isBuildOrTestLog` method. This change might lead to inconsistencies if `file.type` does not always reflect the type of log files correctly, especially since test logs are checked using a regex pattern.","nodes":[{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java--7624:8441","promptId":"#C8X7D","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7624,"endPos":8441,"startLine":202,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":223,"endLineOffset":5,"length":818}]},{"id":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java-10449:10602-","promptId":"#VFJ6X","srcPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","dstPath":"src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/remote/ByteStreamBuildEventArtifactUploader.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10449,"endPos":10602,"startLine":289,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":291,"endLineOffset":5,"length":154}],"dstChanges":[]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":1,"uncoveredGroundTruth":0,"coveredMatchable":15,"uncoveredMatchable":3,"timing":66832,"tokensIn":11942,"tokensOut":966}